WEBVTT

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:03.940
<b>February 18th, 2020</b>

00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:24.160
What's... going on?

00:00:25.850 --> 00:00:26.760
So shaky...

00:00:41.690 --> 00:00:44.980
But I've felt fine ever 
since becoming a zombie...

00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:47.820
Something's happening to my body!

00:00:49.030 --> 00:00:52.090
I have to tell... Kotaro-san...

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:11.960
<b>Zombie Land Saga Revenge</b>

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:15.630
So, it looks like we're adrift.

00:01:15.630 --> 00:01:18.070
Well, that's surprising.

00:01:18.070 --> 00:01:20.680
Where are we even headed?! 
Will we be able to make it back?

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:23.750
Chill out! Even if we sink, 
we won't die! Probably.

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:27.230
Maybe we'll get to a deserted island. 
Then we can go on an adventure!

00:01:27.230 --> 00:01:30.190
Zombie survival, huh? 
Good thinking, shrimpy!

00:01:32.110 --> 00:01:36.200
For now, let's do our makeup so we'll 
be ready for anything that happens.

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:39.790
What a mess...

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:51.950
Damn it! There's no way 
to know what's going on.

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:51.960
<b>Inubashiri 

00:01:54.520 --> 00:01:57.180
This is just like the depopulation.

00:01:57.180 --> 00:02:00.270
The curse that would strike 
Saga when Reiwa begins.

00:02:00.610 --> 00:02:05.700
The fact that we weren't able to settle 
things a year ago, when it was still Heisei...

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:08.310
Has been just as bad as I figured it would.

00:02:08.310 --> 00:02:10.310
We need to get out of here!

00:02:16.820 --> 00:02:19.440
No, no, no, no, no, no, no—

00:02:26.250 --> 00:02:27.960
<b>Hamasaki Beach Park</b>

00:02:26.510 --> 00:02:29.380
This isn't a deserted island. It's Saga.

00:02:29.380 --> 00:02:31.650
Pretty close to where we started out, too.

00:02:31.650 --> 00:02:34.850
Damn, I know there's not exactly 
a ton of people, but...

00:02:34.850 --> 00:02:36.540
What's in that case there, Junko-han?

00:02:36.820 --> 00:02:39.420
The tools for making Ozaki dolls.

00:02:39.420 --> 00:02:41.460
I wanted to make sure they 
didn't get wet, so...

00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:43.880
Always the hard worker.

00:02:45.580 --> 00:02:46.850
What is it?

00:02:52.280 --> 00:02:54.290
It's so old and crummy, it's gonna collapse!

00:02:54.290 --> 00:02:56.600
Oh, man! We've gotta get 
all our crap out of there!

00:03:22.160 --> 00:03:25.340
Our house is gone.

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:29.940
All our costumes... 
and Kotaro-san's instruments...

00:03:30.210 --> 00:03:31.970
And our makeup!

00:03:31.970 --> 00:03:33.020
What do we do?!

00:03:33.020 --> 00:03:36.390
I'm sorry! I should have 
brought that instead!

00:03:37.190 --> 00:03:40.740
Well, things have taken 
a turn for the troublesome.

00:03:40.930 --> 00:03:44.540
So much crazy stuff has happened, 
I can't get worked up about it anymore.

00:03:45.280 --> 00:03:46.800
I have to agree.

00:03:46.800 --> 00:03:50.180
I understand how you feel, but... 
what're we gonna do now?

00:03:50.760 --> 00:03:52.050
Sanko-chan?

00:03:52.780 --> 00:03:54.000
Machiko-san!

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:56.170
What're you gals doing out here?

00:03:56.170 --> 00:03:57.240
Who's that?

00:03:57.240 --> 00:03:59.390
We work together at the factory.

00:03:59.710 --> 00:04:02.000
It, uh, looks like our 
house got swept away...

00:04:02.290 --> 00:04:06.420
That rubble is what's left of your 
house? Oh, gosh, what a mess!

00:04:06.420 --> 00:04:08.610
And when you were all living together...

00:04:08.610 --> 00:04:12.060
You should all come on down to Kation, 
then. It's been turned into a shelter.

00:04:16.870 --> 00:04:18.120
Damn, dude...

00:04:18.120 --> 00:04:20.870
The damage must be even 
worse than we thought.

00:04:20.870 --> 00:04:24.730
The actual shelter was too much 
of a mess to use, so here we are.

00:04:24.730 --> 00:04:26.310
This whole thing's a disaster.

00:04:27.170 --> 00:04:32.280
And we all know it's times like this that 
you have to put on a strong face, but...

00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:34.440
You know how it is.

00:04:34.870 --> 00:04:37.690
I wonder where Kotaro-san is.

00:04:40.600 --> 00:04:43.780
Sorry to stick you all up here, 
but there's no other space.

00:04:43.780 --> 00:04:46.090
Oh, no apologies necessary! 
It's a huge relief.

00:04:46.440 --> 00:04:49.980
You even had tarp to spare. 
We're really grateful.

00:04:49.980 --> 00:04:52.070
Thank you so much!

00:04:52.070 --> 00:04:55.640
Well, with how popular you are, 
it might work out better this way.

00:04:55.640 --> 00:04:58.060
There's cardboard you can lay out 
to sit on and blankets downstairs,

00:04:58.060 --> 00:04:59.540
so come and pick those up later.

00:05:00.020 --> 00:05:02.990
Now, what are your friends' names?

00:05:02.990 --> 00:05:04.820
Uh... well...

00:05:03.840 --> 00:05:05.930
Well, that's Ichiko.

00:05:05.320 --> 00:05:10.580
<b>1-ko</b>

00:05:05.820 --> 00:05:10.580
<b>2-ko</b>

00:05:05.930 --> 00:05:06.770
Niko, here!

00:05:06.770 --> 00:05:10.110
And that's Yonko, Itsuko, and Mutsuko!

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:10.580
<b>4-ko</b>

00:05:08.070 --> 00:05:10.580
<b>5-ko</b>

00:05:08.820 --> 00:05:10.580
<b>6-ko</b>

00:05:10.110 --> 00:05:12.150
Well, that'll be easy to remember!

00:05:12.300 --> 00:05:13.660
I'm Machiko!

00:05:13.660 --> 00:05:15.660
Wait... where's Tae— Err, Zeroko?!

00:05:15.840 --> 00:05:17.660
Huh?! She's gone!

00:05:21.010 --> 00:05:22.730
Here you go.

00:05:24.180 --> 00:05:26.780
Zeroko! You shouldn't eat that!

00:05:27.460 --> 00:05:29.270
We're so sorry...

00:05:29.270 --> 00:05:32.680
Oh, it's totally fine! You girls 
have been through a lot, too.

00:05:32.680 --> 00:05:35.520
She must've been hungry! Eat on up.

00:05:38.660 --> 00:05:41.340
Oh, my, aren't you a hungry little dear!

00:05:42.610 --> 00:05:44.810
I-Is there anything we can help with?

00:05:44.810 --> 00:05:47.120
Oh, we could definitely use a hand!

00:06:10.650 --> 00:06:13.800
Everybody from the factory knows how 
hard a worker you are, Sanko-chan...

00:06:13.800 --> 00:06:16.020
But I guess that goes for all of you!

00:06:16.020 --> 00:06:17.490
Make sure to get rest when you can.

00:06:17.490 --> 00:06:20.580
The rest of us will be in 
trouble without your help!

00:06:20.580 --> 00:06:24.020
Oh, you don't have to worry about us! 
Because we're zombies—

00:06:24.370 --> 00:06:25.530
We're busy like some bees!

00:06:27.390 --> 00:06:30.390
I wanna go home!

00:06:30.630 --> 00:06:33.990
Come on! Come on, please!

00:06:33.990 --> 00:06:37.510
Hey! Hey! I wanna go home!

00:06:51.210 --> 00:06:53.100
One, two, three, four!

00:07:13.750 --> 00:07:19.100
<i>With the crystal clear rivers carrying joy!</i>

00:07:19.100 --> 00:07:24.540
<i>And peace to all around!</i>

00:07:36.350 --> 00:07:39.310
<b>February 20th, 2020</b>

00:07:38.110 --> 00:07:39.300
Ookoba-san!

00:07:39.880 --> 00:07:41.850
I've got a broad idea of what's going on...

00:07:42.020 --> 00:07:43.360
Is it the whole prefecture?

00:07:43.360 --> 00:07:47.250
Yeah. All of Saga and parts of the 
neighboring prefectures have lost power.

00:07:47.250 --> 00:07:49.250
A bunch of towers have been knocked over,

00:07:49.250 --> 00:07:51.380
which means the internet 
and cell phones are down.

00:07:51.380 --> 00:07:55.650
Damn it, this is why I said we should 
get a satellite phone for the office!

00:07:55.650 --> 00:07:57.860
The roads are all a mess, too.

00:07:57.860 --> 00:08:02.180
Sounds like everyone from the worst-hit 
areas is staying in shelters.

00:08:02.850 --> 00:08:04.640
So, should we split up again?

00:08:09.310 --> 00:08:13.040
I'm coming to you from the Kation location in 
Karatsu that has been converted into a shelter.

00:08:14.120 --> 00:08:17.730
I'm with NBK Fukuoka. How are 
things going around here?

00:08:17.730 --> 00:08:20.030
I mean, it's pretty crazy with 
everyone having to stay here!

00:08:20.030 --> 00:08:21.120
It's gotta be, right?!

00:08:21.120 --> 00:08:25.210
This is the biggest shelter in the area,
 so it's like all of Saga's here!

00:08:25.210 --> 00:08:27.260
Not really, though!

00:08:27.260 --> 00:08:30.580
Feels pretty weird, sleeping 
where you used to shop!

00:08:31.430 --> 00:08:34.800
Oh, I'd definitely say I miss my house.

00:08:34.800 --> 00:08:38.680
But everyone's trying their 
best to stay upbeat.

00:08:38.680 --> 00:08:42.360
If it weren't for that, 
I'd have hit my limit already.

00:08:42.650 --> 00:08:45.940
I'm sure of it. So, I'm really grateful.

00:08:46.320 --> 00:08:50.840
W-Well, we're really concerned 
about the kids and the elderly!

00:08:50.840 --> 00:08:53.050
And there's no telling 
how long it'll last...

00:08:53.050 --> 00:08:54.710
We've got a few kids ourselves!

00:08:54.710 --> 00:08:57.480
The youngest is two and she 
really takes after her mom!

00:08:57.720 --> 00:09:01.680
But, y'know, those girls are always 
around to play with them...

00:09:01.680 --> 00:09:03.940
Oh, that's them over there.

00:09:02.780 --> 00:09:04.650
Okay, let's get started!

00:09:06.240 --> 00:09:07.720
Franchouchou?!

00:09:08.260 --> 00:09:10.800
Number Six's star is so cute!

00:09:10.800 --> 00:09:11.830
Isn't it?

00:09:11.270 --> 00:09:12.890
All right, kids, gather around!

00:09:12.890 --> 00:09:14.710
I wonder what song it's gonna be?

00:09:14.710 --> 00:09:16.480
Me, too!

00:09:17.660 --> 00:09:21.370
All right, kiddos, I see this 
is just about everybody!

00:09:21.370 --> 00:09:22.870
No pushing, okay?

00:09:23.140 --> 00:09:27.910
All right, we're gonna sing for you 
guys a bit today, so check it out!

00:09:29.740 --> 00:09:32.120
One, two, three, four!

00:09:32.120 --> 00:09:35.700
<i>Awaken returner! You just have to want it</i>

00:09:35.700 --> 00:09:39.500
<i>A miracle that you're longing to feel!</i>

00:09:40.070 --> 00:09:41.940
<i>Wanna succeed so gotta get it right!</i>

00:09:41.940 --> 00:09:43.720
<i>Never gonna stop, so gotta proceed!</i>

00:09:43.720 --> 00:09:45.100
<i>Giving my all to walk this way!</i>

00:09:45.100 --> 00:09:47.110
<i>Heading straight down the 
path to a gentle future!</i>

00:10:09.800 --> 00:10:11.790
Have you been performing every day?

00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:15.900
Y-Yes! During the day we help out 
with whatever needs to be done,

00:10:15.900 --> 00:10:19.040
and at night we sing and dance a little.

00:10:19.040 --> 00:10:21.810
I saw a lot of smiles. 
They seemed to really enjoy it.

00:10:21.810 --> 00:10:27.160
W-We're just t-trying to do what we can!

00:10:27.750 --> 00:10:29.120
Number Two, you're the group's leader.

00:10:29.640 --> 00:10:31.800
Can you tell us how you 
ended up helping like this?

00:10:32.190 --> 00:10:35.280
Yeah! We're just doing what we gotta do!

00:10:35.280 --> 00:10:38.080
Come on, that's not much of an answer!

00:10:39.530 --> 00:10:43.190
You brought these girls back to life, 
without their permission...

00:10:43.190 --> 00:10:46.950
I'm going to put a stop to you trying to profit off 
these dead girls by making them into idols...

00:10:47.980 --> 00:10:50.530
W-Well, it's like... we 
gotta do what we gotta do!

00:10:50.540 --> 00:10:52.500
<b>February 21st, 2020</b>

00:10:58.220 --> 00:10:59.610
(You okay?!)

00:10:58.510 --> 00:10:59.910
Still alive...

00:11:00.810 --> 00:11:03.330
I'm... not dying...

00:11:04.640 --> 00:11:06.930
Hey, anyone down here?

00:11:06.930 --> 00:11:11.090
Nobody down here? Aw, damn it, 
my pants are soaked through...

00:11:11.330 --> 00:11:14.410
(Hey! We're in here!)

00:11:14.410 --> 00:11:16.510
(We're in here!)

00:11:16.730 --> 00:11:19.480
Wait, you in there? Can you 
try and show me where?

00:11:19.480 --> 00:11:21.410
(We're right over here!)

00:11:21.610 --> 00:11:24.740
Holy crap, there you are! Hang on a sec!

00:11:29.950 --> 00:11:31.650
Please, look after him.

00:11:31.650 --> 00:11:33.220
Sure. What about you?

00:11:33.220 --> 00:11:36.360
I have somewhere I need to go.

00:11:36.360 --> 00:11:39.830
Whoa, wait! I actually 
have a lot of questions—

00:11:39.830 --> 00:11:43.310
I'd tell you not to do anything stupid... 
but you're not gonna listen.

00:11:43.310 --> 00:11:45.040
You're not going to die.

00:11:45.810 --> 00:11:50.280
Franchouchou will save Saga.

00:11:54.850 --> 00:11:56.770
Let's all do our best again today!

00:11:57.110 --> 00:11:58.010
Yeah!

00:12:02.900 --> 00:12:03.710
Huh?

00:12:03.950 --> 00:12:08.930
<b>Zombie Land Saga Revenge</b>

00:12:08.970 --> 00:12:13.960
<b>Zombie Land Saga Revenge</b>

00:12:20.700 --> 00:12:26.410
<i>How long will it take to make real?</i>

00:12:26.410 --> 00:12:29.640
<i>That dream that still feels so vibrant</i>

00:12:30.670 --> 00:12:34.430
<i>Saying you can make it, 
that it's just within reach</i>

00:12:34.430 --> 00:12:39.420
<i>Using those excuses</i>

00:12:34.440 --> 00:12:40.440
<b>The Morning After Torrential Rain</b>

00:12:39.760 --> 00:12:44.900
<i>What can I do before it all falls apart?</i>

00:12:42.360 --> 00:12:44.910
<b>The Morning After Torrential Rain</b>

00:12:45.090 --> 00:12:49.320
<i>Can't let despair block the vision</i>

00:12:47.870 --> 00:12:50.330
<b>The Morning After Torrential Rain</b>

00:12:52.450 --> 00:12:57.330
<i>I'm only hoping for the future</i>

00:12:57.800 --> 00:13:03.290
<i>Fantasies aren't enough 
to push back the darkness</i>

00:13:03.290 --> 00:13:09.050
<i>I want to be able to fight back with reality</i>

00:13:09.050 --> 00:13:14.300
<i>And I can't give up on Saga</i>

00:13:14.300 --> 00:13:20.950
<i>Even if it's a never-ending battle</i>

00:13:22.770 --> 00:13:27.010
Hey, what do you think 
Franchouchou's gonna sing today?

00:13:27.010 --> 00:13:28.250
Good question.

00:13:34.920 --> 00:13:36.050
This is rough.

00:13:36.370 --> 00:13:39.260
It was starting to flake off during work...

00:13:39.260 --> 00:13:41.500
Woulda been real bad news without the mask.

00:13:46.480 --> 00:13:48.810
Romero! Shhh!

00:13:49.050 --> 00:13:53.130
I asked Machiko-san for some makeup, but...

00:13:55.510 --> 00:13:56.910
I knew it.

00:13:56.910 --> 00:13:59.270
It needs to be our special 
makeup, or it won't stay on.

00:13:59.270 --> 00:14:03.180
I get the feeling the remaining patches 
will come off while we're singing.

00:14:03.180 --> 00:14:05.790
Masks won't be much help at that point.

00:14:05.790 --> 00:14:08.500
But everyone's looking forward to it...

00:14:09.690 --> 00:14:11.360
<i>This is what they really look like?</i>

00:14:12.030 --> 00:14:15.240
But... I don't want to just give up.

00:14:16.340 --> 00:14:17.120
Right on.

00:14:17.120 --> 00:14:17.970
Me neither.

00:14:17.970 --> 00:14:20.200
We should keep going if we can find a way.

00:14:20.200 --> 00:14:21.340
I think so, too.

00:14:22.010 --> 00:14:23.610
I feel the same way.

00:14:23.610 --> 00:14:26.180
But... without a way to actually do it...

00:14:26.960 --> 00:14:30.510
Masks to hide our faces would work, but...

00:14:30.510 --> 00:14:34.050
Hey, there are toy stores in the mall, 
right? Maybe they have masks!

00:14:34.050 --> 00:14:35.740
That's a good idea.

00:14:35.740 --> 00:14:38.290
But... the stores are all closed.

00:14:38.290 --> 00:14:39.950
Maybe we should break in!

00:14:39.950 --> 00:14:42.140
That would be more like 
typical zombie behavior.

00:14:42.140 --> 00:14:45.120
Damn it, what're we gonna do?!

00:14:45.120 --> 00:14:48.210
For now, let's get some distance 
from the destructive ideas.

00:14:49.850 --> 00:14:52.030
The paint for the Ozaki dolls...

00:14:52.660 --> 00:14:53.860
That's it!

00:14:54.080 --> 00:14:56.510
If we don't have masks, 
 we can make them!

00:15:17.340 --> 00:15:19.350
What're they trying to do?

00:15:22.240 --> 00:15:24.940
Good evening! We're Franchouchou!

00:15:25.140 --> 00:15:27.720
We're gonna give it our all 
to sing for you tonight!

00:15:27.720 --> 00:15:30.480
So we're counting on you to cheer for us!

00:15:32.700 --> 00:15:34.900
<i>Is this... not working?</i>

00:15:34.900 --> 00:15:37.820
<i>Do these girls think 
about the risks at all?</i>

00:15:38.950 --> 00:15:39.790
It's like these!

00:15:41.370 --> 00:15:42.730
That's right!

00:15:42.730 --> 00:15:43.670
They get it!

00:15:44.240 --> 00:15:45.390
We're clear!

00:15:46.450 --> 00:15:47.780
Nice.

00:15:48.010 --> 00:15:49.160
I think we're good, right?

00:15:49.160 --> 00:15:51.220
It's a better reception 
than I figured we'd get.

00:15:51.220 --> 00:15:52.700
I'm a little worried about 
the bake quality...

00:15:52.700 --> 00:15:54.120
Let's take this as far as we can.

00:15:54.120 --> 00:15:54.970
Go, go!

00:15:54.970 --> 00:15:56.740
It's just our style.

00:15:57.630 --> 00:15:58.900
Ready and...

00:15:58.900 --> 00:16:01.800
We're Franchouchou!

00:16:14.310 --> 00:16:16.360
Crap! Crapcrapcrap!

00:16:16.360 --> 00:16:18.270
I think the openings for the 
eyes made them less durable...

00:16:18.270 --> 00:16:19.500
They weren't baked thoroughly enough!

00:16:19.500 --> 00:16:20.750
That's not really the issue.

00:16:20.750 --> 00:16:23.100
They got a good look at us!

00:16:23.100 --> 00:16:25.520
What do we do? What do we do? 
What do we do? What do we do?!

00:16:26.110 --> 00:16:27.260
<i>They've done it now!</i>

00:16:29.480 --> 00:16:31.570
If it's come to this...

00:16:31.570 --> 00:16:33.290
We don't have any other options. Right?

00:16:34.330 --> 00:16:39.760
Uh... listen... We're sorry 
for hiding it all along.

00:16:44.030 --> 00:16:44.950
We're...

00:16:44.950 --> 00:16:47.060
Did you get hurt?

00:16:48.390 --> 00:16:50.980
Nah, it's not that...

00:16:50.980 --> 00:16:52.030
We're zombies.

00:16:53.450 --> 00:16:56.230
Nuh-uh! Zombies are scary.

00:16:56.230 --> 00:16:57.170
Yeah!

00:16:57.170 --> 00:17:00.570
They're bitey! And dangerous!

00:17:00.760 --> 00:17:04.370
You're not scary, so you're 
not zombies! You're...

00:17:04.370 --> 00:17:06.390
Yeah, that's right!

00:17:08.750 --> 00:17:10.470
You're Franchouchou!

00:17:11.850 --> 00:17:13.800
Yeah, Franchouchou!

00:17:14.240 --> 00:17:15.960
And cute!

00:17:16.400 --> 00:17:17.930
Franchouchou!

00:17:17.930 --> 00:17:26.050
Franchouchou! Franchouchou! 
Franchouchou! Franchouchou!

00:17:26.050 --> 00:17:27.860
Aw, you figured it out!

00:17:27.020 --> 00:17:27.860
Ai-chan?!

00:17:28.220 --> 00:17:32.180
And here we went and got this zombie 
makeup to try to scare you!

00:17:34.250 --> 00:17:36.480
Oh! That's funny!

00:17:36.940 --> 00:17:40.090
Okay, kids, we hope you 
have fun again today!

00:17:40.920 --> 00:17:42.920
Yeah!

00:17:42.920 --> 00:17:50.690
Franchouchou! Franchouchou! 
Franchouchou! Franchouchou!

00:17:50.100 --> 00:17:51.360
All right, everybody!

00:17:51.360 --> 00:17:53.950
We're ready to rock this mall 
again today, so check it out!

00:17:53.950 --> 00:17:55.040
Yeah!

00:18:05.030 --> 00:18:07.110
<i>It's not that they didn't 
consider the risk...</i>

00:18:07.110 --> 00:18:11.920
<i>These girls are risking more than I can 
imagine, every time they get on stage.</i>

00:18:12.220 --> 00:18:14.460
<i>But... they care more about...</i>

00:18:15.800 --> 00:18:18.030
<i>conveying how they feel.</i>

00:18:18.690 --> 00:18:22.480
Those girls... Franchouchou... are idols.

00:18:23.170 --> 00:18:27.330
No matter what state they're in, 
I believe that as they exist now...

00:18:27.330 --> 00:18:29.670
Is the embodiment of true idols.

00:18:31.960 --> 00:18:33.120
Ookoba-san...

00:18:33.840 --> 00:18:37.130
I'd like to ask for your help.

00:18:38.650 --> 00:18:40.590
I thought we were done for...

00:18:40.900 --> 00:18:42.790
We made it through this time...

00:18:42.790 --> 00:18:44.650
Those kids saved us.

00:18:44.650 --> 00:18:48.050
It truly is a blessing to have fans.

00:18:48.050 --> 00:18:50.110
What're we going to do tomorrow, though?

00:18:50.110 --> 00:18:53.040
Let's bake the masks more thoroughly 
so that they're more durable.

00:18:53.040 --> 00:18:54.850
That's not the actual problem.

00:18:54.850 --> 00:18:56.710
I don't know if we have any 
other options, though...

00:18:57.450 --> 00:18:59.570
Get that masked nonsense out of your heads!

00:19:00.090 --> 00:19:01.540
Kotaro-san!

00:19:01.540 --> 00:19:03.890
Where the hell has your shady ass been?!

00:19:03.890 --> 00:19:06.710
Do you realize how much 
trouble we've been through?!

00:19:07.010 --> 00:19:10.830
Ozaki dolls are normally 
made with a lot more care!

00:19:10.830 --> 00:19:12.290
That's... not the actual issue...

00:19:12.290 --> 00:19:14.120
You are so late!

00:19:15.250 --> 00:19:17.420
Oh, pipe down!

00:19:17.420 --> 00:19:19.340
For now, just line up!

00:19:19.690 --> 00:19:22.880
We've gotta do something 
about the way you all look.

00:19:25.210 --> 00:19:27.420
I haven't given up on our revenge.

00:19:27.860 --> 00:19:30.930
We're still having the concert on March 8th.

00:19:31.790 --> 00:19:33.400
Are you serious?

00:19:33.590 --> 00:19:35.780
I think this disaster is exactly 
why it needs to happen.

00:19:38.140 --> 00:19:40.870
Seeing you all has made me sure of that.

00:19:42.970 --> 00:19:46.450
Saga needs to see you singing.

00:19:48.570 --> 00:19:49.910
The adults are waiting.

00:19:52.050 --> 00:19:53.370
So are the children.

00:19:55.520 --> 00:19:56.850
You girls are idols.

00:19:59.080 --> 00:20:03.800
You were able to bring smiles to the people 
here... so I know you can do this.

00:20:07.620 --> 00:20:11.740
That said, we're going to 
be working with a handicap.

00:20:12.690 --> 00:20:15.200
We won't have time for rehearsals 
on the day of the show, either.

00:20:15.820 --> 00:20:18.730
You'll be coming in without 
practice. Are you willing—

00:20:18.730 --> 00:20:19.680
Even so...

00:20:20.150 --> 00:20:26.070
Even so, if that'll help the people of Saga,
 we're willing to risk our lives.

00:20:28.190 --> 00:20:30.000
'Cept your lives are already over.

00:20:30.870 --> 00:20:35.210
On March 8th, sixteen days from now, 
you'll need to assemble at EFS at 10 a.m.

00:20:35.830 --> 00:20:38.500
I'm going to do <i>everything</i>
 I can in the meantime.

00:20:38.970 --> 00:20:42.370
You're gonna do everything zombiely 
possible, and then let the dice fall. Got it?

00:20:45.530 --> 00:20:46.770
Kotaro-san!

00:20:53.430 --> 00:20:54.200
What is it?

00:20:56.410 --> 00:20:59.700
I just... realized I never 
actually told you this.

00:21:00.810 --> 00:21:03.610
All this time, you've never given up...

00:21:03.610 --> 00:21:06.400
Well, except for that one time.

00:21:06.940 --> 00:21:11.520
But even so, we only made it this far 
because you were here to pull us along.

00:21:12.830 --> 00:21:15.930
And now, just like I was moved 
after seeing Ai-chan...

00:21:15.930 --> 00:21:20.640
I met a girl like Maimai-chan,
who felt the same way after seeing me.

00:21:21.540 --> 00:21:26.390
And it's just... I mean, everything's 
been a mess since that rainstorm, but...

00:21:26.390 --> 00:21:28.660
Performing here at the shelter...

00:21:29.230 --> 00:21:33.550
It's like I've found the real reason to sing 
with the others, since becoming a zombie...

00:21:34.160 --> 00:21:36.380
That's what it feels like.

00:21:38.830 --> 00:21:42.970
So, I just... Kotaro-san...

00:21:45.850 --> 00:21:50.220
Thank you for making me an idol!

00:21:57.240 --> 00:21:58.880
Thank you, Inui-kun!

00:22:07.340 --> 00:22:09.600
<b>No matter who hates me for it</b>

00:22:10.350 --> 00:22:12.680
<b>Even if it means taking on god or the devil</b>

00:22:12.680 --> 00:22:14.100
<b>1-48-52 Haneda Southwest
 Suginami, Tokyo 
 ZLS Corporation Inc. 
New Member Audition Submissions 
C/O Audition Office</b>

00:22:14.100 --> 00:22:16.810
<b>I'm doing it!</b>

00:22:18.270 --> 00:22:19.270
I...

00:22:21.140 --> 00:22:22.090
I...

00:22:24.160 --> 00:22:25.200
Kotaro-san?

00:22:25.200 --> 00:22:28.650
I told you, I've got it!

00:22:29.490 --> 00:22:30.610
Listen to me, Sakura!

00:22:30.950 --> 00:22:34.030
I was lying when I said you 
didn't have it, before!

00:22:34.380 --> 00:22:39.570
And as long as Franchouchou exists, 
I'm going to be someone who has it!

00:22:40.120 --> 00:22:44.920
And the truth is, Sakura,
 your dream doesn't end with EFS!

00:22:45.350 --> 00:22:46.490
Your...

00:22:47.260 --> 00:22:48.780
The dream of your entire group!

00:22:48.780 --> 00:22:52.410
Is to become eternal idols 
loved around the globe!

00:22:52.410 --> 00:22:55.760
And until that comes true, Sakura, I...

00:22:56.690 --> 00:22:57.640
I will...

00:22:59.340 --> 00:23:00.130
I'm...

00:23:03.220 --> 00:23:05.610
I'm going to have it, eternally.

00:23:21.960 --> 00:23:24.960
<b>Episode 11</b>

00:23:21.960 --> 00:23:24.960
<b>All It Takes Is for You to Be There SAGA</b>

00:23:24.960 --> 00:23:25.710
<b>Next Episode Preview</b>

00:23:25.720 --> 00:23:26.660
Sakura here.

00:23:26.660 --> 00:23:30.520
If Saga needs us, then we're going 
to sing with everything we've got

00:23:30.520 --> 00:23:32.390
and nothing is going to stop us!

00:23:32.620 --> 00:23:35.140
Next time on <i>Zombie Land 
Saga Revenge</i>, Episode 12:

00:23:35.140 --> 00:23:36.840
"The Greatest SAGA In History."

00:23:35.720 --> 00:23:39.970
<b>Episode 12: The Greatest SAGA In History</b>

00:23:36.840 --> 00:23:38.720
Saga is eternal.
